@leouieda just want to mention that GMT 6.7.0 has just been released and introduces [**-H** for `colorbar`](https://docs.generic-mapping-tools.org/6.7/colorbar.html#h) to not have the automatic scaling of the colorbar font size based on the colorbar width applied:

> From GMT 6.5 on, colorbar annotation fonts are auto-scaled. Use this option to prevent that effect and let user set fonts as they wish.

Maybe this can be helpful and can reduce the confusion. Will need to test this and think about adding an alias for **-H** at https://github.com/GenericMappingTools/pygmt/issues/4243.

Ok, I've done the Zenodo uploads. Have also added the paper DOI under 'Related Works' -> 'Is published in':

